# results/raw/ is contractually "unmodified tool output, committed for traceability"
# (CLAUDE.md, docs/benchmark-philosophy.md). Git's default text handling breaks that
# contract quietly: endpoint-diag captures are `curl -i` dumps whose HTTP response
# headers are CRLF-terminated *because CRLF is the wire format*, and normalising them
# to LF rewrites the evidence on the way into the index. The bytes committed would no
# longer be the bytes captured, and nothing in the artifact would say so.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion outright — no normalisation on add, no
# reconversion on checkout — so every result file round-trips byte-identical on any
# platform. Applied to the whole tree rather than to *.txt because the same guarantee
# has to hold for driver dumps, CSV sidecars and JSON alike; a future tool that emits
# CRLF must not silently lose it for want of a matching pattern here.
results/** -text
enterprise/results/** -text

# Same reasoning for anything a driver writes verbatim.
runtime/drivers/** -text
